# Catalog file format

File: catalog/docs/catalog.oot

The public index is the file named `catalog` at the repo root.
opm fetches `https://catalog.openooda.org/catalog`. Each line is
one package version:

```
name|version|caps|deps|sha256
```

The line ends with a newline. `caps` is a comma list. Empty
`deps` is allowed. `sha256` is 64 lowercase hex digits of the
payload bytes.

`index` is a byte-for-byte copy of `catalog`. `index.minisig` is
the minisign signature of `catalog`. `registry.pub` is the public
key opm pins for the stock origin.

Example:

```
hello|0.1.0|FsRead||6498c89ac067d10897e8eb3dfe2800ace2efa3c3228df2c2a78e9e84bc4019df
echo|0.1.0|FsRead||14d389c387ed6503fd1632236fefaf6608b218ce28c91faa4522ddf409e18446
caps|0.1.0|FsRead||36800f950198935a26fc3808e8f7e52df7fee026f8014d772272f922bfdb0daa
oocat|0.2.5|FsRead,FsWrite,Process,Env,Mcp||06a9c8228154a22f750a67cde856df2f3f49167745f85027670b158bbef9edd5
```

Each package folder is one package. Canonical packages live under
the eight layer directories (`core/`, `kernel/`, `OS/`, `tools/`,
`DE/`, `apps/`, `cloud/`, `agents/`); the root fixtures (`caps`,
`echo`, `hello`) and the seven withdrawn persona folders stay at
the top level. `groups.oot` holds the `@group` install profiles.
A package folder holds `manifest` plus the payload named in
`payload=`. Academy headers are required on the payload. Rebuild
the index from the opm repo:

```
opm bot .
```

Run that with this tree as the target. Then re-sign `catalog`
to `index.minisig` with the catalog minisign key.

Freshness warning: no automated check verifies that `index.minisig`
matches the current `catalog` (a `minisign -V` CI step is ready to
land in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` the moment a fresh signature
exists). Verify by hand after every re-sign
(`minisign -V -p registry.pub -m catalog`). As of 2026-09-27 the
shipped signature (2026-09-04) verifies against NOTHING in history,
not even the bytes committed beside it — it is bogus from birth, not
merely stale. The key holder must re-sign from current `catalog`
before this shelf can be called fully proven. Local use stays
protected by `index.sig` meanwhile. Do NOT build the automated check
on std's ed25519 (verified broken 2026-09-27: hashes hex text instead
of raw bytes, wrong scalar clamp, zero tests); use reference minisign.
